 "stop_rules": {
  "instrument_fault": true,
  "refusal": true,
  "contaminated_redos_max": 3,
  "contaminated_redos_scope": "span",
  "band_unreachable_max": 2,
  "band_unreachable_scope": "span",
  "leg_time_factor": 1.5,
  "notes": "RL-149 section 2.4: REFUSAL, restore unproven, disk or watcher down (span; the lead clears); INSTRUMENT_FAULT (span; the research lead clears); CONTAMINATED_REDOS, 3 in a span (the lead once, then the research lead); LEG_OVERTIME, two legs over 1.5 x their budget in a span (the lead). BAND_UNREACHABLE is dropped; the band_unreachable keys are schema v1 fields that no stop reads. A stop stops the next arm, never a running span. Leg budgets come from the runner's time model by prompt size: 1,076 s (2,000 tokens), 1,156 s (10,000) and 1,251 s (19,458) for a leg that judges its G0 against its own capture (G0 at Part C's 209 s); a span-reference leg's G0 is modeled at 600 s (1,467 s, 1,547 s and 1,642 s), so a span-reference G0 that runs to its 1,200 s cap alone never trips LEG_OVERTIME. leg_budget_s is their ceiling and leg_worst_case_s (a G0 at its 1,200 s cap, with margin) is each leg's process cap."
 },
